## Step 6: Cartographic Visualization

Classification Schemes:

For Mean Layer (0–769 mm):
- 0–50 mm (light yellow) = Arid
- 50–100 mm (yellow) = Semi-arid
- 100–200 mm (light blue) = Moderate
- 200–400 mm (blue) = Wet
- 400+ mm (dark blue) = Very wet

For Slope Layer (−0.5 to +1.2 mm/year):
- <−0.3 (red) = Rapidly drying
- −0.3 to 0 (orange) = Moderately drying
- 0 to +0.3 (yellow) = Stable
- +0.3 to +0.8 (light green) = Moderately wetting
- >+0.8 (dark green) = Rapidly wetting

